<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 377 0 R
/E (A software process model is an abstract, simplified representation of a software development process. It defines the activities, tasks, roles, and sequence of steps involved in building software from the initial gathering of requirements through design, implementation, testing, deployment, and ongoing maintenance. These models serve as a roadmap that development teams follow to ensure software is produced in an organized, repeatable, and quality-assured manner.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
