611 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (The Construction phase is the third and often longest stage of the Rational Unified Process where the software is built incrementally through multiple development iterations. Each iteration involves design, coding, testing, and integration, resulting in a progressively more complete and functional version of the product.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 397 0 R
/T (Transition Phase)
/E (Transition Phase)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
613 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (The Transition phase is the final stage of the Rational Unified Process where the software is delivered to end users in a production environment. This phase includes activities such as deploying the system, migrating data from legacy systems \(if applicable\), conducting user training, creating user documentation, and fixing defects discovered after deployment.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
