<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1438 0 R
/E (Complexity: RUP is often described as "heavyweight." It requires a significant amount of expertise to set up and manage correctly, which can be overwhelming for smaller teams.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1439 0 R
/E (Resource Intensive: Because it demands detailed documentation and specialized roles \(like separate architects and process engineers\), it can consume a lot of time and man-hours.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
630 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1440 0 R
/E (Not Beginner-Friendly: To get the most out of RUP, team members need to be well-versed in UML \(Unified Modeling Language\) and the specific RUP methodology. The learning curve is quite steep.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
631 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1441 0 R
/E ("Analysis Paralysis": There is a risk that the team spends too much time on the Inception and Elaboration phases \(planning and modeling\) and not enough time actually writing the code.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
632 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1442 0 R
/E (Cost: Due to the need for specific tools \(like IBM Rational tools\) and the overhead of managing the process, RUP can be significantly more expensive than "leaner" methods like Agile.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
